# Publish everything

If the user asks to **publish everything**, **publish all**, **deploy all**, **deploy everything**, or redeploy Tune Book + YogApp / Synthesized Yoga together:

1. Run from the abc2book repo root (do **not** invent a parallel deploy path):

```bash
npm run publish:everything
```

Optional flags the user may want:

- `--dry-run` — print steps only
- `--force` — rebuild/redeploy everything (ignore change detection)
- `--no-android` — skip Android APK builds
- `--no-locale-audio` — skip packing/uploading YogApp language packs
- `--no-resolver` — skip Cloud Run light resolver deploy
- `--no-push` / `--no-commit` — build without publishing (also skips locale-audio upload and hosted resolver deploy)
- `--install` — require a plugged-in phone (fail if none); default is auto-install when adb sees a device
- `--no-install` — skip phone install even if a device is connected
- `--wait-pages` — poll GitHub Pages after push

Script: `scripts/publish-everything.sh`

**Change-aware by default:** skips YogApp/Tune Book Android, web/Pages, and Cloud Run resolver when the relevant source paths are clean and already match upstream. Locale audio **packs/uploads only zips whose contents changed** (SHA-256 vs the `audio-v1` release; source-tree digests reuse local zips). Use `--force` for a full rebuild/republish.

It can build Synthesized Yoga (yogapp) Android, Tune Book Android, Tune Book web (embeds `/yoga/`), deploy the hosted Cloud Run light resolver (`local-resolver/deploy-cloud-light.sh` → `tunebook-resolver-light`), publish YogApp locale audio to the `audio-v1` GitHub Release, commit, and push **yogapp** then **abc2book** so https://tunebook.net/ and https://tunebook.net/yoga/ update (non-English / extra-English voice packs download from `https://tunebook.net/yoga/audio-packs/v1/`; GitHub Release `audio-v1` is an optional backup).

If an Android phone is plugged in (adb `device`), it also **re-syncs the just-built web into both Capacitor APKs**, `adb install -r` Synthesized Yoga + Tune Book, and best-effort clears WebView cache so the on-phone web UI matches the publish. Peppertrees (home Docker) and the score-convert sidecar are not redeployed by this script.
